WEBVTT

00:46.920 --> 00:48.010
Emily.

01:02.660 --> 01:05.410
This can't end yet.

01:06.170 --> 01:08.170
Not until I meet you.

01:31.020 --> 01:31.920
Are you all right?

01:31.920 --> 01:33.480
Wh-Wh-What...

01:33.910 --> 01:36.240
What do you think you're doing?!

01:37.260 --> 01:37.950
Huh?

03:09.040 --> 03:13.040
Episode 14

03:09.040 --> 03:13.040
Meeting the Traveler

03:15.530 --> 03:17.550
Why would you do that?!

03:19.290 --> 03:20.070
Huh?

03:20.470 --> 03:23.230
You attacked a Workshop patrol.

03:23.230 --> 03:26.410
Do you have any idea what
will happen to you?

03:26.410 --> 03:27.260
No.

03:27.260 --> 03:29.060
If you do that...

03:30.240 --> 03:31.490
They're already here!

03:32.610 --> 03:35.080
For now, we should run! Follow me!

03:46.410 --> 03:50.050
A Blue Dog. It's up to level 30.

03:50.050 --> 03:51.620
Did you say "level"?

03:51.930 --> 03:56.360
When robots are destroyed, stronger robots
are programmed to come after you.

03:56.360 --> 03:57.590
Then...

03:58.290 --> 04:03.970
I appreciate you rescuing me, but now I'm
being chased by an even stronger patrol.

04:04.670 --> 04:07.920
We can't fight a Blue Dog.

04:08.280 --> 04:10.020
Then what should we do?

04:10.710 --> 04:11.700
Give me a minute.

04:12.330 --> 04:14.350
Traveler
Where should I go?

04:13.830 --> 04:14.350
Emily
Go to D-52.

04:15.260 --> 04:17.860
All right. Follow me.

04:36.410 --> 04:38.500
What is this?

04:39.010 --> 04:40.850
A jamming device.

04:41.560 --> 04:46.980
It disrupts the flow of Shinsu and blocks
radio waves broadcast to a certain area.

04:46.980 --> 04:48.260
Then...

04:48.660 --> 04:53.260
If we block the signal, we won't be
pursued by an even stronger patrol.

04:53.260 --> 04:54.890
That's amazing.

04:55.710 --> 04:59.270
Then we should defeat
that patrol robot here.

04:59.270 --> 05:01.430
Defeat it?

05:01.430 --> 05:04.900
Blue Dogs are on another level from
that hunk of junk you fought earlier.

05:05.650 --> 05:09.390
You'd need to be at least as
strong as a Princess of Jahad

05:09.390 --> 05:11.570
or a Slayer Candidate to fight one.

05:12.410 --> 05:16.220
If you don't want to die,
help me set up this trap.

05:21.490 --> 05:23.520
Could you put this over there?

05:24.030 --> 05:25.220
Okay.

05:27.910 --> 05:29.270
What are you doing?

05:29.630 --> 05:31.430
Sending a thank-you message.

05:31.430 --> 05:36.440
Traveler
Where should I go?

05:31.430 --> 05:36.440
Emily
Go to D-52.

05:31.430 --> 05:36.440
Traveler
Thanks for all your help.

05:37.440 --> 05:38.840
Now for our next story.

05:39.250 --> 05:43.150
We interviewed Princess Endorsi,
the favorite to win the upcoming battle.

05:43.950 --> 05:46.570
Why participate in the Workshop Battle?

05:46.570 --> 05:49.060
Do I need a reason?

05:49.060 --> 05:51.490
I just felt like it.

05:51.490 --> 05:54.080
Isn't that right, everyone?

05:55.580 --> 05:58.080
Any opponents you have your eye on?

05:59.360 --> 06:02.300
I know exactly what you want me to say.

06:02.300 --> 06:03.960
Jue Viole Grace.

06:03.960 --> 06:05.840
That's the answer you want, isn't it?

06:07.090 --> 06:09.100
Then I'll say it.

06:09.100 --> 06:12.230
It seems like everyone's scared
of him, but don't worry.

06:12.230 --> 06:17.800
I, Endorsi Jahad, will give Jue Viole
Grace the beating of a lifetime!

06:19.100 --> 06:21.470
Endorsi!

06:21.470 --> 06:24.680
L-O-V-E Endorsi!

06:24.680 --> 06:28.030
Pretty and cute Endorsi!

06:28.030 --> 06:30.370
This is giving me second-hand embarrassment.

06:28.030 --> 06:33.570
L-O-V-E Endorsi! Endorsi!

06:30.370 --> 06:33.340
What do people like about her?

06:34.280 --> 06:36.900
Shiny and sparkly Endorsi!

06:36.900 --> 06:40.030
Love you forever, Endorsi!

06:40.030 --> 06:41.790
There are two such idiots right here.

06:41.790 --> 06:44.290
So, why are you in my room?

06:44.290 --> 06:48.070
This is Princess Endorsi, my fave!

06:48.070 --> 06:50.730
Yeah, I got that already. Now get out.

06:50.730 --> 06:53.330
Seriously? You ate my share.

06:53.330 --> 06:55.530
You even ate it with sauce.

06:55.530 --> 06:58.200
I paid for it.

07:01.740 --> 07:03.930
Are you ignoring the others?

07:04.330 --> 07:08.050
You're their leader. You should
pay more attention to them.

07:08.050 --> 07:09.430
Not my problem.

07:09.430 --> 07:15.330
Those cold-hearted jerks ditched me
while I was sleeping to go have fun.

07:17.220 --> 07:20.330
Anyway, wouldn't you say we get along?

07:20.330 --> 07:22.820
Well, we share the same fave.

07:22.820 --> 07:25.260
Then let's watch a movie together.

07:25.890 --> 07:27.420
Good idea!

07:27.420 --> 07:31.600
Why did they gather us here two days
before the floating ship departs?

07:32.080 --> 07:33.770
Are they planning something?

07:34.840 --> 07:36.870
Jue Viole Grace?

07:37.330 --> 07:39.510
He's no big deal.

07:39.830 --> 07:43.440
He's just one of many Regulars, right?

07:43.770 --> 07:47.340
He's still a terrible liar.

07:50.760 --> 07:53.690
Huh? Did you press the wrong button?

07:53.690 --> 07:55.700
I didn't press anything yet.

07:57.210 --> 08:04.340
Hello to the 1,488 Regulars who
have come to the Workshop.

08:04.720 --> 08:09.860
I am Io, one of the hosts
running this Workshop Battle.

08:10.270 --> 08:12.230
A host?

08:13.010 --> 08:18.930
Are you enjoying the beautiful
nightscapes of Sephia island?

08:20.100 --> 08:21.720
Even in the Middle Area,

08:21.720 --> 08:26.610
the beaches of Sephia Island are
famous for their exceptional beauty.

08:26.610 --> 08:29.440
Why not pay them a visit?

08:30.410 --> 08:33.280
Seriously? He interrupted
my interview for this?

08:33.570 --> 08:39.790
But for those of you waiting to depart,
perhaps this is all a bit boring.

08:40.410 --> 08:45.180
So I've arranged for you to play a game
for a boarding pass onto the Archimedes<i>,</i>

08:45.180 --> 08:47.290
which will depart two days from now.

08:47.290 --> 08:48.540
What?

08:48.540 --> 08:49.800
A game?

08:54.300 --> 08:55.680
Say what?

08:56.290 --> 08:58.040
So that's how it is.

08:58.930 --> 09:06.150
Use the items I'm about to distribute
to win a spot on the Archimedes<i>.</i>

09:06.960 --> 09:08.670
The rules of the game are...

09:08.670 --> 09:10.110
What is this?

09:10.110 --> 09:11.520
One shot...

09:14.550 --> 09:15.520
A gun?

09:15.870 --> 09:17.450
One opportunity!

09:20.430 --> 09:23.800
The One Shot, One Opportunity Game.

09:25.210 --> 09:28.410
There are 248 boarding passes.

09:29.380 --> 09:32.470
If you defeat a Regular using
the guns I distributed,

09:34.460 --> 09:37.060
you'll be transported to the Archimedes<i>.</i>

09:38.520 --> 09:40.850
Each person gets one bullet.

09:42.710 --> 09:45.750
If you miss, you're out.

09:46.240 --> 09:49.750
You can also steal guns from your opponents.

09:51.250 --> 09:53.220
Guns can be loaded with up to six bullets.

09:53.650 --> 09:56.860
After the first shot,
the selection lever is activated.

09:56.860 --> 09:58.920
There is a dark mode and a light mode.

10:00.230 --> 10:04.030
Getting hit by a light shot will
transport you to the Archimedes<i>.</i>

10:10.210 --> 10:13.210
The first person to get shot
will receive a Blood Tamara.

10:13.880 --> 10:17.920
The person who sends the most
participants to the Archimedes<i></i>

10:17.920 --> 10:20.930
using light shots will receive
a White Heavenly Mirror.

10:21.890 --> 10:27.020
Additionally, defeating the "Bongbong"
fairies of happiness flying around the island

10:27.020 --> 10:31.000
will earn you both a boarding
pass and a super rare item.

10:31.900 --> 10:33.900
Give it a shot.

10:34.790 --> 10:40.150
The game will begin in one minute
when the safeties are released.

10:48.240 --> 10:51.070
In other words, we either
use these to shoot Regulars

10:51.070 --> 10:54.640
or shoot our teammates with stolen bullets.

10:55.550 --> 10:58.440
Dark shots are high-risk.

10:58.440 --> 11:02.360
Light shots are more certain.

11:02.360 --> 11:06.100
If you're lucky, you can even get an item.

11:07.090 --> 11:09.600
We'll start by collecting bullets.

11:16.600 --> 11:18.210
Let's move.

11:18.210 --> 11:22.110
We need to stake out a spot before
the safeties are released.

11:23.290 --> 11:25.120
That won't be necessary.

11:33.380 --> 11:36.740
Hey, you can't be serious.

11:38.030 --> 11:43.390
What's more valuable? You or a Blood Tamara?

11:45.480 --> 11:47.460
See you later, Wangnan.

11:49.140 --> 11:50.640
Start

12:13.130 --> 12:15.300
Two bullets secured.

12:15.810 --> 12:16.860
Nice work.

12:20.080 --> 12:24.460
Your real scream got us two bullets.

12:24.460 --> 12:28.990
Screams make people panic.
It clouds their judgment.

12:28.990 --> 12:30.920
You really scared me!

12:30.920 --> 12:32.810
You should've told me beforehand!

12:34.020 --> 12:37.800
Dan, do you think he could've acted
that convincingly if I'd told him?

12:38.920 --> 12:40.050
Damn it!

12:40.050 --> 12:44.570
Being on your team is going
to give me a heart attack!

12:46.720 --> 12:50.200
Khun, Wangnan, is everyone okay?

12:50.840 --> 12:52.320
We're fine over here.

12:52.320 --> 12:53.210
How about you?

12:53.570 --> 12:56.960
We can't get in touch with Prince or Miseng.

12:57.280 --> 13:00.830
What? I thought you guys were together.

13:00.830 --> 13:05.360
Those two are afraid of heights, so we split up.

13:07.250 --> 13:08.130
Wangnan.

13:09.520 --> 13:14.120
Want to try something a bit stupid?

13:18.890 --> 13:19.950
Damn it!

13:19.950 --> 13:22.480
People have been dropping like
flies since the game started.

13:22.480 --> 13:23.590
This is bad.

13:23.940 --> 13:27.570
They probably shot their
teammates for the item.

13:27.570 --> 13:29.800
Yeah, probably.

13:29.800 --> 13:33.550
Sticking together as a team seems
like a disadvantage in this game.

13:33.890 --> 13:36.990
Though if you can collect enough
bullets to board together,

13:36.990 --> 13:40.340
you might be recognized as a true team.

13:40.340 --> 13:44.630
More importantly,
there's something on my mind.

13:44.630 --> 13:45.590
Can I ask you something?

13:45.850 --> 13:48.340
Sure, what is it?

13:49.440 --> 13:52.540
Why did you find rooms to rent so far away?!

13:54.350 --> 13:56.740
They had the nicest view!

13:56.740 --> 13:58.620
There are no other guests, either.

13:58.620 --> 14:00.130
We're not here on vacation.

14:00.130 --> 14:03.220
If we can't get enough bullets,
I'm shooting you first.

14:03.990 --> 14:06.110
Anyway, what about the guys who were out?

14:06.110 --> 14:08.600
I sent Vespa.

14:08.960 --> 14:10.510
They'll be fine.

14:10.510 --> 14:12.880
I'm more worried about Endorsi.

14:12.880 --> 14:16.690
Since Bam died, she's become
even more self-centered.

14:20.920 --> 14:22.570
E-Endorsi.

14:22.570 --> 14:26.060
Hello, peasants. Your princess has arrived.

14:26.060 --> 14:27.600
Where have you been?

14:27.600 --> 14:29.040
What do you mean?

14:29.680 --> 14:33.240
I was off collecting bullets for you guys.

14:33.240 --> 14:35.040
What? Bullets?

14:36.420 --> 14:37.730
Ta-da!

14:37.730 --> 14:40.670
Four?! Where did you find them?

14:40.670 --> 14:43.380
I think they're called paparazzi.

14:43.380 --> 14:47.350
I caught them sneaking around
trying to take my picture.

14:47.350 --> 14:48.330
Damn it!

14:48.330 --> 14:52.040
How dare you insult noble
journalists like us?!

14:52.500 --> 14:53.500
Shut up!

14:53.500 --> 14:56.550
You got caught trying to snap
a picture of my underwear!

14:56.550 --> 14:59.960
If you don't want to die,
hand over your bullets!

15:00.190 --> 15:02.430
Why would they take a picture of that?

15:02.430 --> 15:04.200
I wanna see that photo so bad.

15:04.200 --> 15:05.960
They're true journalists.

15:09.970 --> 15:11.940
That's four bullets for us.

15:11.940 --> 15:14.470
We might finish pretty quickly.

15:14.470 --> 15:17.430
Damn you cowards.

15:17.430 --> 15:18.240
Huh?

15:18.240 --> 15:22.660
You boasted about catching
Viole for the Regulars,

15:22.660 --> 15:27.230
but instead you've stolen bullets
from decent people like us.

15:28.630 --> 15:33.670
How could you attack us when there are
FUG members staying at a nearby hotel?

15:33.670 --> 15:37.620
We'll leak this to the press and
expose you, you savage princess!

15:39.380 --> 15:41.530
From now on, we're on Team Viole!

15:41.530 --> 15:42.620
What?

15:42.990 --> 15:45.170
Go, go, Viole!

15:45.170 --> 15:47.730
Love you forever, FUG!

15:47.730 --> 15:48.690
FUG?

15:50.590 --> 15:51.760
You guys...

15:54.320 --> 15:56.350
Where are they?

15:56.350 --> 15:58.210
In a nearby hotel.

15:58.620 --> 15:59.300
Is that true?

15:59.300 --> 16:01.070
D-Definitely.

16:01.070 --> 16:04.270
We're journalists. Don't underestimate
our information network.

16:06.420 --> 16:07.650
What should we do?

16:10.650 --> 16:13.070
The number of available
boarding passes is dropping.

16:13.070 --> 16:16.660
If we want to make it through this game
unscathed, we'll have to put up with them.

16:17.610 --> 16:18.660
But...

16:20.150 --> 16:23.410
Let's go put a bullet in their heads.

16:30.170 --> 16:32.090
Take your positions.

16:32.090 --> 16:33.820
I'll give the orders.

16:33.820 --> 16:36.180
We're going to hunt some FUG.

16:37.310 --> 16:39.070
I'm not putting up with them.

16:40.530 --> 16:41.400
Let's go.

16:45.940 --> 16:49.250
P-Princess, how was that?

16:49.250 --> 16:52.940
My acting was perfect, wasn't it?

16:54.690 --> 16:56.560
It was all right.

16:56.560 --> 16:59.680
Anyway, that information is good, right?

16:59.680 --> 17:02.550
Of course. No doubt about it.

17:02.960 --> 17:07.800
I saw Jue Viole Grace leave with my own eyes.

17:07.800 --> 17:10.860
I see. Then I'll let them handle the nobodies.

17:10.860 --> 17:14.310
P-Princess? What about the
photos you promised?

17:14.310 --> 17:15.720
Princess?

17:15.720 --> 17:20.720
Endorsi
Where is Jue Viole Grace?

17:15.720 --> 17:20.720
Emily
Go to D-52.

17:17.040 --> 17:20.290
I'm off to enjoy the main dish.

17:21.250 --> 17:23.140
Viole is missing?

17:23.140 --> 17:25.730
How could you neglect to watch him?

17:25.730 --> 17:27.720
He didn't want us to.

17:27.720 --> 17:30.210
And you thought that would be okay?

17:30.550 --> 17:33.820
We can't get in touch with him,
and we don't know where he went.

17:33.820 --> 17:35.990
How will you take responsibility for this?

17:36.820 --> 17:38.700
That's enough.

17:39.480 --> 17:41.010
Reflejo.

17:41.540 --> 17:43.150
What is it, Yuto?

17:43.150 --> 17:45.640
There's a Regular on the
light tower out front.

17:45.640 --> 17:46.710
What?

17:46.710 --> 17:49.940
They're just a Regular. No matter.

17:49.940 --> 17:53.130
They're no ordinary Regular.

17:57.150 --> 17:58.590
It's Anaak Jahad.

18:05.090 --> 18:06.780
They seem to have noticed us.

18:06.780 --> 18:08.150
We're not going in?

18:08.600 --> 18:10.840
There's no need to rush.

18:10.840 --> 18:14.250
We'll scare them while we wait
for the others to arrive.

18:14.250 --> 18:16.440
I want to collect bullets in the meantime.

18:17.670 --> 18:22.430
Where did Endorsi wander off to, anyway?

18:25.970 --> 18:27.630
When will we enter?

18:30.130 --> 18:33.550
When there are fewer than
100 boarding passes left.

18:34.920 --> 18:36.960
That's when we'll go in.

18:38.590 --> 18:40.950
She hasn't done anything yet.

18:41.430 --> 18:43.670
She must have realized we don't have bullets.

18:43.670 --> 18:47.390
She's waiting to attack until we're
under as much pressure as possible.

18:47.920 --> 18:51.110
Why did we have to encounter her now?

18:51.520 --> 18:54.400
Our exit has been blocked.
What do you intend to do?

18:55.090 --> 18:57.170
We'll wait for Viole to return.

18:57.170 --> 18:59.610
The longer we wait,
the greater our disadvantage.

18:59.610 --> 19:03.090
We can't leave this place without Viole.

19:03.610 --> 19:05.660
What if he doesn't come back?

19:06.590 --> 19:10.610
If that happens, I'll kill everyone.

19:13.850 --> 19:15.680
When there are less than 100.

19:18.960 --> 19:22.630
When there are less than 100, it's on.

19:25.460 --> 19:28.190
I think I got it.

19:28.190 --> 19:29.560
Really?

19:29.560 --> 19:31.710
Hey, nice!

19:31.710 --> 19:34.230
I'm impressed you could manage that.

19:34.230 --> 19:35.160
Thank you.

19:35.820 --> 19:38.850
Oh, right. I haven't told you my name yet.

19:39.220 --> 19:44.450
Call me Traveler. What's your name?

19:45.100 --> 19:47.720
I-I'm the 25th Bam.

19:47.720 --> 19:50.960
Th-The 25th Bam?

19:53.730 --> 19:56.810
Were you about to ask me something?

19:57.790 --> 20:00.230
Why were you being chased by that patrol?

20:00.860 --> 20:02.970
Did you do something bad?

20:04.280 --> 20:08.480
I tried to sneak onto the <i>Archimedes</i>.

20:09.610 --> 20:11.060
Why would you do that?

20:14.310 --> 20:15.990
I'm trying to save someone.

20:17.440 --> 20:19.550
The person I love is in there.

20:44.340 --> 20:48.870
I have to save her before
the Workshop Battle ends

20:49.690 --> 20:53.430
because the grand prize of
this Workshop Battle...

20:55.000 --> 20:56.270
is a human being.

21:00.740 --> 21:03.250
No way! They found us already?

21:05.330 --> 21:09.080
Bam, I'll trigger the
explosion as they come in!

21:13.160 --> 21:16.080
Three, two, one!

21:16.080 --> 21:17.630
Fire in the hole!

21:34.390 --> 21:36.030
Damn. It didn't work.

21:36.690 --> 21:37.760
We have to run!

21:37.760 --> 21:40.020
We can't beat it in a fair fight!

21:40.570 --> 21:45.240
If it has a shield, then I'll wait for
the moment that machine attacks.

22:10.010 --> 22:12.220
What? Endorsi?

23:47.440 --> 23:50.540
Love you forever, Endorsi.

23:49.090 --> 23:51.250
Next Time
The Promise of That Day
